<section class="jn-sec" aria-labelledby="jn-faq-h">
    <div class="jn-sec-head"><div><h2 class="jn-h" id="jn-faq-h">Honest answers</h2></div></div>
    <div class="nn-faq">
        <details>
            <summary>What exactly arrives in my Personal feed?</summary>
            <p>One episode each morning: the day's real episodes of the shows
               you picked, in your order, joined by Mira's short spoken handoffs.
               Nothing is summarized: you hear the full episodes, minus the
               cross-promo tails that don't make sense mid-edition. If you set a
               length or turn on Skip repeats, Mira leaves out whole chapters
               (a story you already heard today, say) and tells you which.
               Chapters mark every segment so you can skip freely.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>How do I add it to my podcast app?</summary>
            <p>From your account: one tap opens your feed in Apple Podcasts,
               Overcast, Pocket Casts, Castro, AntennaPod or Podcast Addict. On a
               computer, scan the code with your phone. Any other app that takes
               a feed URL works too; the URL is yours alone, so sharing it shares
               your subscription.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>How does the Local morning brief stay honest?</summary>
            <p>Weather comes from measured forecast data for your city. The
               local story is found with a live web search and Mira names the
               source out loud. On a day with nothing verifiable worth your
               time, she says so and moves on, no filler, ever.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>Can I cancel easily?</summary>
            <p>Yes. Billing is by Stripe with self-serve cancellation, one
               click, no email required. Your private feed runs to the end of
               the paid period, and your lineup stays saved on your free
               account if you ever come back.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>Is this AI-generated?</summary>
            <p>Yes. The shows are written and voiced with AI from the day's
               sourced reporting, and every episode says so on air. A person
               chooses each show's sources and rules and fixes what goes wrong,
               but no one reads every episode before it ships; every claim is
               checked against its source and an unverified one is marked
               publicly. Mira is an AI anchor and is always introduced as one.
               The full policy is at
               <a href="{{ path_prefix }}ai-disclosure.html">our AI disclosure</a>.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>What happens with my email and city?</summary>
            <p>Your email is your account and newsletter address. It's never
               sold, and only the services that run your account see it. Your first name, city, subjects and note to Mira
               exist only so Mira can greet you and build your edition: they're
               stored with your account, sent to the AI model that writes
               Mira's lines each morning (xAI, never with your email), never
               published, and deleted with your account. The lineup you build
               on this page stays in your browser until you create the account. The
               <a href="{{ path_prefix }}privacy-policy.html">privacy policy</a>
               has the details.</p>
        </details>
    </div>
</section>

